  "source_feature_observations": {
    "title_credit_matter": "All 15 members have pre-envelope title and Alexander Maclaren author lines, English language statements, and contributor/production credit lines. PG header/title material is distinguished from original publisher/imprint evidence; it does not by itself identify the precise printed edition or establish constituent-work roles.",
    "contents_and_internal_boundaries": "CONTENTS occurs at the per-member line positions above, sometimes twice within one PG member. PG 7925 has internal volume headings at lines 56 and 10994; PG 8200 has internal volume headings at lines 57 and 12248. PG 7069 has another CONTENTS at line 10438 and a source-uppercase book boundary THE BOOK OF EXODUS at line 10441. PG 24674 has another CONTENTS at line 11618 and source-uppercase boundaries THE FIRST EPISTLE OF PETER at line 11621, THE SECOND EPISTLE OF PETER at line 11668, and THE FIRST EPISTLE OF JOHN at line 11687. These are retained as source text/style and are not used to infer individual exposition boundaries.",
    "uppercase_lines": "The census counts a nonblank line with at least one alphabetic character whose stripped text equals its uppercase form. Many are contents entries, book/volume labels, wrappers, or headings; the census is descriptive and is not a sermon count or selector.",
    "paragraphs_and_blank_lines": "Blank-line-delimited prose is retained in order. The cohort contains 36,845 exact-empty lines and 120 nonempty whitespace-only lines; both classes are represented, not collapsed or discarded.",
    "notes_and_inline_markers": "Seven lines contain bracketed decimal markers: four in PG 15836 (two anchors and two matching source note-definition lines) and three in PG 13601 (two heading occurrences and one prose occurrence, with no matching definition line found in that member). The route preserves the bracketed strings in place and does not infer note attachment. The underscore_delimited_inline_span_count is a same-physical-line regex census only; some underscore pairs cross wrapped lines. The route preserves every literal underscore and does not strip or reflow these source markers.",
    "page_and_license_material": "Every member has one ordered Project Gutenberg START and END wrapper and a FULL LICENSE marker after the END line; all pre-envelope, wrapper, and post-envelope lines are represented. The retained text provides no page-image/page-sequence crosswalk; print-page identity remains unresolved rather than inferred from line numbers.",
    "source_errors_and_special_characters": "PG 8070 contains U+2014 EM DASH in the all-caps source lines at 86 and 10589; preserve the retained character and do not silently repair it."
  },
